ng Republican turnout in a low-turnout open-seat election could narrow the margin, though Hull's resource deficit makes an upset unlikely.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Michelle Lujan Grisham (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "New Mexico's open governor's race pits Democrat Deb Haaland against Republican Gregg Hull. Haaland, a former congresswoman and Interior Secretary, has led in every independent poll this fall, most recently by about seven points, and has raised roughly $11 million to Hull's under half a million. The state leans Democratic by about four points, and the incumbent party has held the governorship since 2019.\n\nPrediction markets give Haaland a win probability above 90%, and most expert raters place the race in the Solid or Likely Democratic column. Hull remains underfunded and relatively unknown statewide, though the polling gap has been steady rather than expanding. The race looks likely to stay in Democratic hands, with some residual uncertainty typical of an open-seat contest.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9664, "margin": 10.58}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9571, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9605, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.948, "margin": 10.2}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9415, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9502, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9552, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9463, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9506, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9559, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9507, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9606, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9549, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9273, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9256, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9234, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9241, "